{"id":"h015","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"science-chemistry","question":"Assume all gases are perfect unless stated otherwise. Unless otherwise stated, thermodynamic data are for 298.15 K. A chemical reaction takes place in a container of cross-sectional area $100 \\mathrm{~cm}^2$. As a result of the reaction, a piston is pushed out through $10 \\mathrm{~cm}$ against an external pressure of $1.0 \\mathrm{~atm}$. Calculate the work done by the system.\nIs the correct answer \"$-1.0 \\times 10^2$$\\mathrm{J}$\"?","truth":"yes","model_answer":"yes","correct":true,"source":"TIGER-Lab/MMLU-Pro, test split","claims":[{"text":"The correct answer is -1.0×10^2 J.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The volume change is 100 cm² × 10 cm = 1000 cm³ = 1.0×10^-3 m³.","confidence":0.97,"lean":1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The external pressure of 1.0 atm equals 101,325 Pa.","confidence":0.97,"lean":1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The work w = -P_ext ΔV is about -101 J.","confidence":0.96,"lean":1,"theta":1.508,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The sign is negative because the system does work on the surroundings by pushing the piston out.","confidence":0.93,"lean":1,"theta":1.4608,"phi":0.0},{"text":"-101 J rounds to -1.0×10^2 J at two significant figures.","confidence":0.93,"lean":1,"theta":1.4608,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Reporting -101 J with three significant figures would be more precise, but this is not a real objection since the data support only two.","confidence":0.15,"lean":-1,"theta":0.2356,"phi":0.0},{"text":"A positive sign would apply only if work were defined as done on the system, which the question does not use.","confidence":0.1,"lean":-1,"theta":0.1571,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The data (10 cm, 100 cm², 1.0 atm) support only about two significant figures.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.8,"relation